CHAPTER III
RIGHTS OF VICTIMS
Article 4
(1) Every victim of gender-based violence and child victim of violence has the right to:
a. obtain protection for personal, family, and property security, and freedom from threats related to information that will be, is being, or has been provided;
b. participate in the process of selecting and determining the form of protection and security support;
c. obtain information regarding case developments and court decisions;
d. obtain integrated services that are fast, appropriate, comfortable, and in accordance with needs;
e. recovery and social reintegration;
f. obtain legal, psychological, spiritual guidance, economic, social assistance and interpreter;
g. special handling related to victim confidentiality;
h. obtain guarantees of their rights related to their status as wife/mother, husband/father, child and household member as well as community member; and
i. obtain information about laws and regulations that protect victims.
(2) The rights of victims as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be implemented in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

CHAPTER II
PRINCIPLES AND OBJECTIVES
Article 2
The protection of victims of gender-based violence and children is based on Pancasila and grounded in the 1945 Constitution, as well as basic principles that include:
a. non-discrimination;
b. best interests of the victim;
c. gender justice and equality;
d. victim protection;
e. maternal survival;
f. child survival and development;
g. respect for the child's opinion;
h. transparency;
i. integration;
j. not blaming the victim;
k. victim confidentiality; and
l. decision-making in the hands of the victim.

REGENT OF SUKOHARJO
REGIONAL REGULATION OF SUKOHARJO REGENCY
NUMBER 6 YEAR 2011
CONCERNING
THE IMPLEMENTATION OF PROTECTION FOR VICTIMS OF
GENDER-BASED VIOLENCE AND CHILDREN
BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD
THE REGENT OF SUKOHARJO,

Considering : a. that all forms of violence, especially gender-based violence and violence against children are violations of human rights and crimes against human dignity as well as forms of discrimination;
b. that victims of gender-based violence and violence against children must receive protection, both from the regional government and/or the community in order to be protected and free from violence and/or threats of violence within the household and community sphere;
c. that based on Law Number 23 Year 2002 concerning Child Protection and Law Number 23 Year 2004 concerning the Elimination of Domestic Violence, the Regional Government together with the community is obligated to undertake prevention, protection, and recovery efforts for victims of gender-based violence and violence against children;
d. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b and letter c, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning the Implementation of Protection for Victims of Gender-Based Violence and Children;

In View of : 1. Law Number 13 Year 1950 concerning the Establishment of Regency Regions within the Province of Central Java;
